\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The drainhole ($\eta _0=2$, $\gamma =-\pi $) and symmetric ($\eta _0=1$, $\gamma =0$) families across the spin range, against $v_e$: (a) the mass $M=\mu _+$ of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end, the angular momentum and the equatorial throat radius; (b) $J/M^2$ against the Kerr bound; (c) the end-mass ratio $M_-/M_+=\mu _-/\mu _+$, which changes sign along the drainhole family at $v_e=0.72$ (dotted), with the backgrounds of the 3D runs (squares); in the shaded band ($v_e=0.46$--$0.70$) the far end has negative mass and the throat does not collapse, and the 3D evolution breaks down before $t=150$ at the puncture $r=0$ into which the far end is compactified; (d) the flattening $R_p/R_e$; (e) the exotic matter: the phantom field's integrated null-energy violation over the $t=\,$const slice per equatorial throat radius, $\mathcal  {I}=\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ (\rho +p_\eta )\,dV/R_e$~\cite  {visser2003} ($\rho $: energy density, $p_\eta $: radial pressure), relative to the static member's $\mathcal  {I}_{\rm  static}$, with the 3D runs (squares) placed by the scalar charge measured on each run's own $t=0$ slice, which reproduces its background's to $3\times 10^{-4}$; (f) the throat angular velocity, which peaks and falls to zero at extremality. Both families end on extremal Kerr, and the faster they spin, the less exotic matter each unit of throat radius needs.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:trends}{{3}{5}{The drainhole ($\eta _0=2$, $\gamma =-\pi $) and symmetric ($\eta _0=1$, $\gamma =0$) families across the spin range, against $v_e$: (a) the mass $M=\mu _+$ of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end, the angular momentum and the equatorial throat radius; (b) $J/M^2$ against the Kerr bound; (c) the end-mass ratio $M_-/M_+=\mu _-/\mu _+$, which changes sign along the drainhole family at $v_e=0.72$ (dotted), with the backgrounds of the 3D runs (squares); in the shaded band ($v_e=0.46$--$0.70$) the far end has negative mass and the throat does not collapse, and the 3D evolution breaks down before $t=150$ at the puncture $r=0$ into which the far end is compactified; (d) the flattening $R_p/R_e$; (e) the exotic matter: the phantom field's integrated null-energy violation over the $t=\,$const slice per equatorial throat radius, $\mathcal {I}=\int (\rho +p_\eta )\,dV/R_e$~\cite {visser2003} ($\rho $: energy density, $p_\eta $: radial pressure), relative to the static member's $\mathcal {I}_{\rm static}$, with the 3D runs (squares) placed by the scalar charge measured on each run's own $t=0$ slice, which reproduces its background's to $3\times 10^{-4}$; (f) the throat angular velocity, which peaks and falls to zero at extremality. Both families end on extremal Kerr, and the faster they spin, the less exotic matter each unit of throat radius needs}{figure.3}{}}
