\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The $(2,0)$ wave of the unperturbed rotating collapse. (a)~$r\,\Delta \psi _4^{20}$ of the D21 run on the $L=128$ box, on spheres $R=14$--45 against retarded time $t-R$. (b)~The wave against spin at $R=14$, each run on its own collapse clock $u=t-R-t_{10}$ ($t_{10}$: the time its equatorial deficit passes $10\%$); the static run (D0) is drawn at zero, its measured record below $3\times 10^{-8}$. (c)~The radiated energy $E_{20}=\tfrac  {1}{16\pi }\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ |\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ r\psi _4\,dt'|^{2}\,dt$ over the aligned burst, per unit $M_{\rm  ADM}$, at $R=18$ (filled) and $R=14$ (open). (d)~The speed of each extremum between neighbouring spheres, against the local coordinate speed of light (crosses). The burst's energy grows with spin, and the static collapse radiates nothing.}}{7}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:wave}{{5}{7}{The $(2,0)$ wave of the unperturbed rotating collapse. (a)~$r\,\Delta \psi _4^{20}$ of the D21 run on the $L=128$ box, on spheres $R=14$--45 against retarded time $t-R$. (b)~The wave against spin at $R=14$, each run on its own collapse clock $u=t-R-t_{10}$ ($t_{10}$: the time its equatorial deficit passes $10\%$); the static run (D0) is drawn at zero, its measured record below $3\times 10^{-8}$. (c)~The radiated energy $E_{20}=\tfrac {1}{16\pi }\int |\int r\psi _4\,dt'|^{2}\,dt$ over the aligned burst, per unit $M_{\rm ADM}$, at $R=18$ (filled) and $R=14$ (open). (d)~The speed of each extremum between neighbouring spheres, against the local coordinate speed of light (crosses). The burst's energy grows with spin, and the static collapse radiates nothing}{figure.5}{}}
